# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# The ascii-check gate rejects a carriage return on purpose, so a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true must not rewrite text files to CRLF.  With
# this file git stores LF and checks out LF on every platform, and a file
# added on Windows is committed with LF.  `text=auto` still lets git treat a
# binary file as binary, so an image or an archive is untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
